{
 "_about": "Bands of ink **inside a zone** that a human has ruled are not a dropped line. Two dispositions: without `covered_by` the ruling says the ink is not type — a printed rule, a footnote separator, a smudge the zoning covers. With `covered_by: N` it says the ink IS type and IS keyed, in line N, whose box strangled it; a clipped folio is the standing case. Each carries the reason it was ruled so, and each is scoped to its own band: exempting a whole page would hide the next dropped line on it. A matched band still reports, flagged `exempted` and carrying its note. This is the *line* layer; ink outside every zone is the zoning's question and lives in gt/zones/_ink_exempt.json. Keyed PP-NNN.",
